  "discussion": {
   "office": "GJT",
   "issued": "2026-11-27T18:04:00+00:00",
   "key_messages": "- Snow will begin along the northern Divide this evening, lingering through Sunday morning. Snow totals of 10-15 inches are expected for the Park and Elkhead mountains, with 4-8 inches across the Flat Tops and Central Divide Mountains.\n- Winds gusting 40 to 50 mph are expected with this system this evening through Saturday night, leading to blowing and drifting snow and difficult driving conditions over the mountain passes.\n- An unsettled pattern looks to continue into next week with potential for more mountain snow by mid week, but details remain uncertain."
